<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<rdf:RDF
   xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
   xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/"
   xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
   xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
   xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
   xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
   xmlns:vann="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/"
>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/MaximumAllowableThreshold">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Maximum allowable threshold</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Short-term limit (e.g. MAC-EQS); may be compared against a single observation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/NoThresholdDefined">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">No threshold defined</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Case (a): the regulation sets no limit for this analyte in this matrix.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/IndeterminateCompliance"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Threshold</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A concentration limit set by a regulation, together with the conditions under which it may lawfully be applied.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b39"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b40"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b41"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/aggregationFunction">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">aggregation function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Function used to combine group members, e.g. sum for the 24-PFAS standard.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/GroupThreshold"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/AggregationFunction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b47">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/MaximumAllowableThreshold"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b48"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/NotCoveredBySurvey">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Not covered by survey</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The regulation defines a threshold for an analyte the
monitoring programme never measured. Under a closed-world model this is
invisible; here it is an explicit verdict, which is what makes "assess a 2018
survey under a 2026 regulation" a well-posed question.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/IndeterminateCompliance"/>
    <skos:example xml:lang="en">A survey that measured none of the 24 PFAS named by the 2026 standard cannot report compliance with their sum; the aggregate is not assessable rather than zero.</skos:example>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/PreconditionUnmet">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Precondition unmet</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Case (c): a required applicability condition is not satisfied.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/IndeterminateCompliance"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/requiresCondition">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">requires condition</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A precondition of the threshold. Unmet preconditions yield no verdict, not a default pass.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/ApplicabilityCondition"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/Analyte">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Analyte</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A substance whose concentration is the observed property.
Aligned to ChEBI/PubChem with skos:exactMatch rather than renamed, so that two
regulation packages referring to the same substance resolve to one IRI — the
precondition for comparing them.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/complianceDeadline">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">compliance deadline</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Date by which member states or operators must meet the standards; may be long after entry into force.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/appliesToGroup">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">applies to group</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The substance group whose aggregate the threshold constrains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/GroupThreshold"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/SubstanceGroup"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/Compliant">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Compliant</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Compliance is established: it holds for every value consistent with the observation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/ComplianceOutcome"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b17"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b4">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:minCardinality>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/usedProcedure"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/Campaign">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sampling campaign</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bounded sampling exercise. Making it explicit lets the same station be compared across time and prevents campaigns being conflated.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/inForceFrom">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">in force from</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Date of entry into force. Observations predating it can still be assessed against the package, but the result is counterfactual and must be labelled as such.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/transcriptionStatus">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">transcription status</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Whether a value has been verified against the primary legal
text. Machine-readable so that unverified values can be excluded from analysis
rather than trusted by default.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/TranscriptionStatus"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/SubstanceGroup">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Substance group</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of analytes assessed collectively, e.g. 'pesticides total', 'sum of 24 PFAS'.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/definedBy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">defined by</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The legal instrument establishing the threshold. Mandatory: an uncited threshold cannot be defended.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Regulation"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/producedByRun">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">produced by run</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a result to the analytical run that produced it, and so to the limits actually in force for that measurement.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/AnalyticalRun"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"/>
    <dcterms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-08-03</dcterms:created>
    <dcterms:creator rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b1"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">CENSO extends SOSA/SSN with detection and quantification
limits, interval-valued results, applicability conditions on regulatory
thresholds, and a three-valued compliance assessment in which "cannot be
determined" is an explicit, queryable outcome, subtyped by the reason it cannot. Designed for measurement
processes in which non-detection is the normal result and must be represented as
an open-world upper bound rather than as zero.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">CENSO: an ontology for censored environmental observations</dcterms:title>
    <vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>censo</vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>
    <vann:preferredNamespaceUri>https://w3id.org/censo/</vann:preferredNamespaceUri>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/"/>
    <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/1.0.0"/>
    <owl:versionInfo>1.0.0</owl:versionInfo>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/requiresCompleteGroup">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">requires complete group</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">True when every group member must have been measured for the
aggregate to be assessable. If members are missing from the monitoring panel,
the aggregate is `censo:IndeterminateCompliance`, not a partial sum. The 24-PFAS
sum is the obvious case: a survey that measured none of them cannot report
compliance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/GroupThreshold"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b21">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b23"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b27">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">0.0</owl:hasValue>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/resultLowerBound"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/HardnessClassCondition">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hardness class condition</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The threshold varies by water hardness class, as for cadmium.
Without a hardness measurement the applicable class — and therefore the
applicable threshold — is unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/ApplicabilityCondition"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/ComplianceOutcome">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Compliance outcome</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The verdict of comparing an observation against a threshold.
THREE-valued: the standard is met, it is not met, or compliance cannot be
determined. The three are what the Directive itself admits, and the third is
what closed-world models cannot express. The reason a verdict cannot be
determined is carried by the subclasses of IndeterminateCompliance rather than
by a fourth top value, which would assert a distinction the Directive does not
make.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b32"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/AssessedObservation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Assessed observation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An observation whose detection status has been determined; the union of the four statuses.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b2"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b3"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b4"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b5"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/PossibleExceedance">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Possible exceedance</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The interval straddles the threshold; the measurement
cannot decide. A subclass of IndeterminateCompliance recording that the reason
is the width of the interval, not a defect of the record: unlike the other
three, this observation was measured, reported and assessable, and the method
still could not answer the question.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/IndeterminateCompliance"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b13"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/appliesToAnalyte">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">applies to analyte</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The substance constrained. Group thresholds use cereg:appliesToGroup instead.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Analyte"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/runUsedMethod">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">run used method</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The method this run executed; the run inherits its limits, which may then be overridden per run.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/AnalyticalRun"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/AnalyticalMethod"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b9">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/UnresolvedObservation"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Concept</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reused from SKOS; declared here only so that this standalone distribution is self-describing.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/CensoredAmbiguous">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Censored ambiguous</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Case (f): the observation is censored and the threshold lies within [0, LOD], so non-detection is compatible with both compliance and exceedance. Stated at the DETECTION limit; no monitoring release read here reports one, so the class is part of the vocabulary and not of the results.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/IndeterminateCompliance"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">was derived from</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reused from PROV-O; declared here only so that this standalone distribution is self-describing.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b10">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:unionOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b11"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/limitUnit">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">limit unit</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Unit of LOD and LOQ. Mandatory: a bare limit is not comparable to anything.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/AnalyticalMethod"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b17">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b19"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">Vocabulary for expressing environmental quality
standards as self-contained, versioned, swappable modules, including group and
derived thresholds such as a total-pesticide sum.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">CENSO-REG: pluggable regulation packages for censored observations</dcterms:title>
    <vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>cereg</vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>
    <vann:preferredNamespaceUri>https://w3id.org/censo/reg/</vann:preferredNamespaceUri>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/"/>
    <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/1.0.0"/>
    <owl:versionInfo>1.0.0</owl:versionInfo>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b55">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/EstimatedObservation"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b56"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/determinesAnalyte">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">determines analyte</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The analyte this method measures. One method may cover many analytes, each with its own limits, so limits are asserted per method-analyte pair.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/AnalyticalMethod"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Analyte"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b8">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/QuantifiedObservation"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b9"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/BoundNotEstablished">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Bound not established</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Case (e): the record establishes no bound to compare against
the threshold. Either nothing says whether the number is a measurement — neither
a censoring flag nor a limit is reported, so no interval can be built — or the
number contradicts the limit reported beside it. The distinction from
MethodInsufficient matters: there the bound is known and known to be too wide,
here there is no bound at all, and the two call for different repairs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/IndeterminateCompliance"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/belowThreshold">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">below threshold</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Materialised when resultUpperBound &lt;= thresholdValue.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/assessableAgainst"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/MatrixCondition">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Matrix condition</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Restricts the threshold to a matrix: inland surface water, coastal water, biota, sediment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/ApplicabilityCondition"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/calibrationR2">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">calibration coefficient of determination</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">R² of the calibration curve; a quality indicator for the reported limits.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/AnalyticalMethod"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Person">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Person</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reused from FOAF; declared here only so that this standalone distribution is self-describing.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/AggregationFunction">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Aggregation function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">How the members of a substance group are combined into the single quantity the threshold applies to.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/AnalyticalMethod">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Analytical method</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A procedure determining the concentration of an analyte,
characterised by a limit of detection and a limit of quantification. The limits
belong to the METHOD, not to the substance: the same analyte may be censored at
one laboratory and quantified at another. Attaching limits to the analyte — the
common shortcut — makes cross-laboratory comparison unsound.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b36"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b37"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Procedure"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sosa:Procedure with a detection limit.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/EstimatedObservation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Estimated observation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Detected, but between LOD and LOQ, so the reported magnitude
is indicative only. Reporting it as a point estimate overstates what the method
supports. Datasets frequently contain such values presented as if quantified.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b41">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/definedBy"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b30">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onClass rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/SubstanceGroup"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/appliesToGroup"/>
    <owl:qualifiedCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:qualifiedCardinality>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b3">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:minCardinality>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/atStation"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/definesThreshold">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">defines threshold</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a package to the thresholds it establishes. The inverse direction (threshold to package) goes through censo:definedBy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/definedBy"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/exceeds">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">exceeds</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Materialised when resultLowerBound &gt; thresholdValue: exceedance holds for every value consistent with the observation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/assessableAgainst"/>
    <owl:propertyDisjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/belowThreshold"/>
    <owl:propertyDisjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/possiblyExceeds"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Regulation package</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A self-contained set of thresholds attributable to one legal
instrument at one point in time. Assessment is always relative to a package;
there is no such thing as an unqualified compliance verdict.

A package is a censo:Regulation -- the same legal instrument, at the granularity
at which it is versioned, cited and swapped. Declaring them separate classes
made cereg:definesThreshold and censo:definedBy incoherent as inverses, which
OOPS! reported as a critical pitfall and which is why an individual previously
had to be typed as both.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b38"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Regulation"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b5">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:unionOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b6"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/AnalyticalRun">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Analytical run</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">One execution of an analytical method on a batch of samples,
carrying its own calibration curve and therefore its own detection limits. Two
observations of the same analyte are only strictly comparable when they share a
run, or when the runs' limits are known and comparable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/NonRelevantMetabolite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Non-relevant metabolite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Metabolite without the parent's pesticidal activity; brought into scope by the 2026 EU update under a separate standard.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Analyte"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/transposes">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">transposes</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">National package implementing a supranational one, e.g. YSKY transposing the EU EQS Directive. Divergences between the two are meaningful and queryable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b56">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/QuantifiedObservation"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b57"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b40">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/thresholdUnit"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/resultUpperBound">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">result upper bound</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Largest concentration consistent with the observation; the LOD when censored.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/calibrationSlope">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">calibration slope</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Slope of the calibration curve, from which LOD and LOQ are derived.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/AnalyticalMethod"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b15">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b16"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/ApplicabilityCondition">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Applicability condition</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A condition that must hold before a threshold may be applied to an observation.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/Exceedance">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Exceedance</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Exceedance is established: it holds for every value consistent with the observation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/ComplianceOutcome"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b21"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/thresholdUnit">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">threshold unit</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Unit of the threshold; must be commensurable with the observation unit before comparison.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b37">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/limitUnit"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b51">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/possiblyExceeds"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b52"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/Sum">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/AggregationFunction"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">sum</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b43">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/atStation"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b44"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/Jurisdiction">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Jurisdiction</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A legal territory in which a regulation package applies, identified by an ISO 3166 code or by 'EU'.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Procedure">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Procedure</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reused from SOSA; declared here only so that this standalone distribution is self-describing.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RelevantMetabolite">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Relevant metabolite</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Metabolite retaining the pesticidal activity of its parent; assessed as a pesticide.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Analyte"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/NonRelevantMetabolite"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b61">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/Assessment"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b62"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/conditionSatisfied">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">condition satisfied</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Materialised by the rule layer when the observation demonstrably meets the condition.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/ApplicabilityCondition"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/DetectedObservation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Detected observation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The analyte was found, whether or not it could be quantified.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/CensoredObservation"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b10"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/productIon">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">product ion (Q3) m/z</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Mass-to-charge ratio of the product ion monitored in the third quadrupole; together with the precursor it identifies the transition.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/MassSpectrometryTransition"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/assessableAgainst">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">assessable against</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Materialised when EVERY condition the threshold requires is
satisfied for this observation. Only then may a verdict be drawn. Universal
quantification over a materialised set is a closed-world check, so it lives in
SHACL, not in OWL.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/derivedFromRecord">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">derived from record</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links an observation to the source file, sheet and cell it was extracted from, so every assertion is traceable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/supersedes">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">supersedes</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Names the package this one replaces. Transitive, so the full amendment chain is queryable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b38">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:minCardinality>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/sourceDocument"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/GroupThreshold">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Group threshold</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A threshold applying to an aggregate over a substance group rather than to one analyte.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b30"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b31"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/possiblyExceeds">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">possibly exceeds</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Materialised when resultLowerBound &lt;= thresholdValue &lt; resultUpperBound: the interval straddles the limit.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/assessableAgainst"/>
    <owl:propertyDisjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/belowThreshold"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/BioavailabilityCondition">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Bioavailability condition</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The threshold is a bioavailable concentration (as for nickel,
lead, copper and zinc under EU EQS) and requires hardness, dissolved organic
carbon and pH for normalisation. Absent those covariates, no compliance
statement is possible.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/ApplicabilityCondition"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/retentionTime">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">retention time</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Chromatographic retention time used to confirm analyte identity within the run.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/MassSpectrometryTransition"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Unit</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reused from QUDT; declared here only so that this standalone distribution is self-describing.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b63">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/TranscriptionStatus"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/jurisdiction">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">jurisdiction</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The legal territory in which the package applies (ISO 3166 code or 'EU').</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/Jurisdiction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/UnresolvedObservation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Unresolved observation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Made, but its detection status cannot be established, typically
because the applicable LOD/LOQ for the analyte-method pair is unknown. Such
observations are structurally undecidable and must be excluded from inference
rather than silently treated as quantified.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b25"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b2">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onClass rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Analyte"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/hasAnalyte"/>
    <owl:qualifiedCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:qualifiedCardinality>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/QuantifiedObservation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Quantified observation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Detected at or above the limit of quantification; the magnitude is usable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/assessedUnder">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">assessed under</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The regulation package an assessment was carried out against. Mandatory: a verdict without a named package is not interpretable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/Assessment"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/MassSpectrometryTransition">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Mass spectrometry transition</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An LC-MS/MS multiple-reaction-monitoring transition —
precursor and product ion, retention time and the voltages that select them.
It identifies the measurement channel that produced a result, and hence which
detection limit applies. This is the level at which analytical provenance
actually lives, and it is absent from every water ontology surveyed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/AnalyticalMethod"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Observation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reused from SOSA; declared here only so that this standalone distribution is self-describing.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:hasKey rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b42"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b59">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b60"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#hadPrimarySource">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">had primary source</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reused from PROV-O; declared here only so that this standalone distribution is self-describing.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/Regulation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Regulation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dated, versioned legal instrument. Thresholds must cite one, because they change.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b32">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:unionOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b33"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b16">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b14"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b1">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Person"/>
    <foaf:name>Recep Can Altınbağ</foaf:name>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/FractionCondition">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Fraction condition</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Restricts the threshold to an analytical fraction, typically
DISSOLVED for metals. Comparing a total-metal measurement against a
dissolved-fraction threshold is invalid; where the fraction is unrecorded, the
assessment is undecidable rather than conservative.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/ApplicabilityCondition"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/precursorIon">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">precursor ion (Q1) m/z</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Mass-to-charge ratio of the precursor ion selected in the first quadrupole.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/MassSpectrometryTransition"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/duringCampaign">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">during campaign</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The sampling campaign the observation belongs to; part of the observation's identity key.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Campaign"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/resultLowerBound">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">result lower bound</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Smallest concentration consistent with the observation; 0 when censored.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema11-2/#decimal"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b49">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AllDisjointProperties"/>
    <owl:members rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b50"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b12">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/QuantifiedObservation"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/smiles">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">SMILES</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Structure string; supports structural grouping and QSAR-derived properties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Analyte"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b54">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/CensoredObservation"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b55"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/metaboliteOf">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">metabolite of</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Degradation or transformation product. Relevant because a
survey may measure a metabolite while the regulated parent is absent from the
panel, or vice versa. The 2026 EU update explicitly brings non-relevant
pesticide metabolites into scope, so this relation carries legal weight.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Analyte"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Analyte"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso xml:lang="en">Transitive: a transformation product of a transformation product is still one of the parent. NOT symmetric, despite the scanner's suggestion -- the relation has a direction.</rdfs:seeAlso>
    <skos:example xml:lang="en">1-Hydroxyibuprofen metaboliteOf Ibuprofen.</skos:example>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/exceeds"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/assessmentOutcome">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">assessment outcome</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The verdict produced, one of the four compliance outcomes defined in CENSO core.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/Assessment"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/ComplianceOutcome"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/hasAnalyte">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has analyte</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The substance this observation is about; exactly one.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Analyte"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b35">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/IndeterminateCompliance"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reportedValue">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">reported value</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The number as it appears in the source record, kept verbatim for
provenance. Never use it directly in inference: in many datasets a reported 0 is
a non-detection, not a measured zero.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/censoringRecovered">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">censoring recovered</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">True when the detection status was RECONSTRUCTED after the
fact, typically because the source recorded a non-detection as 0 and the status
was recovered by joining the analyte's LOD. Such observations carry an extra
assumption and must remain distinguishable from those whose censoring was
recorded at source.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b62">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/AggregationFunction"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b63"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b33">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Exceedance"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b34"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b60">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/SubstanceGroup"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b61"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/analysedSample">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">analysed sample</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The physical sample analysed. Reuses sosa:Sample so the sampling chain stays in the standard vocabulary.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/AnalyticalRun"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sample"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/memberOfGroup">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">member of group</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Membership in a collectively assessed set. Group membership is curated knowledge with provenance, not a spreadsheet column.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Analyte"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/SubstanceGroup"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b26">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/assessableAgainst"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/inForceUntil">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">in force until</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Date the package ceased to apply. Absent means still in force.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/ToxicEquivalentSum">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/AggregationFunction"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">toxic equivalent sum</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Potency-weighted sum, as used for dioxin-like compounds.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b6">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/CensoredObservation"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b7"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Activity</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reused from PROV-O; declared here only so that this standalone distribution is self-describing.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/TranscriptionStatus">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Transcription status</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">How reliably a threshold value was copied from its legal source. Machine-readable so unverified values can be excluded from analysis rather than trusted by default.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/CensoredObservation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Censored observation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The analyte was sought and not detected. Asserts only that the
true concentration lies in [0, LOD]. It does NOT assert absence. Storing such an
observation as 0 destroys the distinction and biases every derived aggregate
downwards.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b27"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b28"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Observation whose result is below the method's limit of detection.</skos:definition>
    <skos:example xml:lang="en">Atrazine sought and not detected by a method whose limit of detection is 0.02 µg/L: the concentration lies in [0, 0.02], which is not the same claim as zero.</skos:example>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b11">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/EstimatedObservation"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b12"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b48">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/ClassBoundaryThreshold"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b36">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/limitOfDetection"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sample">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sample</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reused from SOSA; declared here only so that this standalone distribution is self-describing.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b22">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/exceeds"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/groupCoverage">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">group coverage</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fraction of a group's members actually measured. Materialised per assessment; reported alongside every aggregate verdict.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/Assessment"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/Maximum">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/AggregationFunction"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">maximum</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/thresholdValue">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">threshold value</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The numeric limit, meaningful only with its unit and applicability conditions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b44">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/duringCampaign"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/regulationVersion">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">regulation version</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Amendment identifier, so thresholds of different vintages stay distinguishable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Regulation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/sourceDocument">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">source document</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Dereferenceable URI of the legal text the values were transcribed from. Required: a threshold without a traceable source is not usable in a regulatory context.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#hadPrimarySource"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b31">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onClass rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/AggregationFunction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/aggregationFunction"/>
    <owl:qualifiedCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:qualifiedCardinality>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/limitOfQuantification">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">limit of quantification (LOQ)</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Lowest concentration measurable with stated accuracy and precision.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/AnalyticalMethod"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/Assessment">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Assessment</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The act of evaluating observations against one regulation
package, producing compliance outcomes. Reified so that the same observations
assessed under two packages yield two comparable, separately attributable
results.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b18">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/belowThreshold"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b39">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:cardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:cardinality>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/thresholdValue"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/limitOfDetection">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">limit of detection (LOD)</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Lowest concentration reliably distinguishable from a blank.
Below it, presence can be neither asserted nor denied. Expressed in
censo:limitUnit.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/AnalyticalMethod"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/FeatureOfInterest">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Feature of interest</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reused from SOSA; declared here only so that this standalone distribution is self-describing.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b20">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b18"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/casNumber">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CAS registry number</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Preferred join key across heterogeneous sources; more reliable than trade or trivial names.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Analyte"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Observable property</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reused from SOSA; declared here only so that this standalone distribution is self-describing.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b19">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b20"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/atStation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">at station</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Where the sample was taken.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/FeatureOfInterest"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b52">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/belowThreshold"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b14">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/possiblyExceeds"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/AnnualAverageThreshold">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Annual average threshold</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Long-term limit (e.g. AA-EQS). Applies to a temporal mean, not
to a single sample; comparing one grab sample against it is a category error that
this class exists to make visible.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/legalReference">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">legal reference</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Citation as published, e.g. 'OJ L 348, 24.12.2008' or 'Resmî Gazete 28483'.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/RegulationPackage"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/requiresCovariate">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">requires covariate</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An observable property that must be co-measured for the condition to be evaluable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/ApplicabilityCondition"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b13">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b15"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/ClassBoundaryThreshold">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Class boundary threshold</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Boundary between water quality classes. Conventional
determinands such as COD, ammonium and phosphate are assessed against these, not
against an EQS — a distinction routinely lost when both are stored as a single
"limit" column.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Threshold"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b45">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AllDisjointClasses"/>
    <owl:members rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b46"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b24">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b22"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b34">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/Compliant"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b35"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/Unverified">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/TranscriptionStatus"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">unverified</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/ArithmeticMean">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/AggregationFunction"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">arithmetic mean</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/VerifiedAgainstPrimarySource">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/TranscriptionStatus"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">verified against primary source</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Entity</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reused from PROV-O; declared here only so that this standalone distribution is self-describing.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b53">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AllDisjointClasses"/>
    <owl:members rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b54"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b50">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/exceeds"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b51"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b58">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AllDisjointClasses"/>
    <owl:members rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b59"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b42">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/hasAnalyte"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="na46cb6a162df4fb9b4552551bedb0c38b43"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/TranscribedFromSecondarySource">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/reg/TranscriptionStatus"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">transcribed from secondary source</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Taken from a project spreadsheet, report or database rather than the legal text. Treat as provisional.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/MethodInsufficient">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Method insufficient</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Case (b): the observation is CENSORED and its
limitOfQuantification exceeds the thresholdValue, so Article 3(3b) of Directive
2008/105/EC provides that the result "shall not be considered" for status
assessment. The censoring condition is part of the case: a quantified result
above the standard is evidence of exceedance whatever the method's limit was, and
is not set aside by this provision.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/IndeterminateCompliance"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/censo/IndeterminateCompliance">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Indeterminate compliance</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">No compliance statement is supportable. The third of the
three outcomes the Directive admits, and the only one a two-valued schema has
nowhere to put. It is ABSTRACT in practice: every instance carries one of the
subclasses below, which record WHY no statement is supportable —

(a) NoThresholdDefined  — the regulation sets no limit for this analyte here;
(b) MethodInsufficient  — the observation is censored and the method's LOQ
    exceeds the threshold, so compliance cannot be demonstrated even in
    principle;
(c) PreconditionUnmet   — a precondition is unmet: unknown fraction, missing
    bioavailability covariates, unknown hardness class;
(d) PossibleExceedance  — the result was measured and assessable, and its
    interval straddles the limit, so the method cannot decide either way;
(e) BoundNotEstablished — the record states no bound to compare at all;
(f) CensoredAmbiguous   — censored with the threshold inside [0, LOD], the
    narrower case at the DETECTION limit, which no monitoring release states.

Case (b) is the sharpest: a laboratory can report "not detected" for a substance
whose LOQ is a hundredfold above the legal limit, and a closed-world system
records that as compliance.

PRECEDENCE. A censored result whose LOQ exceeds the threshold has an interval
that straddles it too, so (b) and (d) both describe it. Article 3(3b) is
decisive — the result "shall not be considered" — and such an observation is
recorded under MethodInsufficient. This is a rule-layer priority and NOT an
owl:disjointWith axiom between the two: the same observation may legitimately be
MethodInsufficient against one jurisdiction's standard and PossibleExceedance
against another's, and class-level disjointness would forbid the two-regulation
assessment this vocabulary exists to support. Exclusivity lives where it always
has, on the comparison properties, per observation-threshold pair.

NOTE ON INFERENCE. This class cannot be defined as "neither of the other two",
because under the open-world assumption an unasserted property is not a false
one. It is materialised under a locally closed world; see censo-shapes.ttl.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/censo/ComplianceOutcome"/>
    <skos:example xml:lang="en">Imidacloprid measured by a method quantifying at 2.065 µg/L against an EU annual-average standard of 0.0068 µg/L: no result the method could return would decide compliance.</skos:example>
  </rdf:Description>
